# frozen_string_literal: true

#
# Api::ApplicationController
# Base controller for all API endpoints under the Api namespace.
# Inherits from Rarchitecture::ApplicationController::API,
# which provides JSON-oriented behavior, standardized RESTful actions,
# and service-based orchestration.
#
# Features:
# - Centralized error handling (rescue_from StandardError with JSON output)
# - Standard RESTful actions: index, show, create, update, destroy
# - Input validation (permitted_params, validate!)
# - Service layer delegation (service, query_params)
# - Output formatting (output, default_output, render_json, render_json_array, render_error, render_empty_json)
# - Authorization helpers (authorize!)
# - Logging and failure capture (log_error, halt!)
# - Pagination helpers (limit, offset, current_page, total count)
#
# Use this as the common ancestor for all API controllers to ensure
# consistent JSON responses, error handling, and service-driven architecture.
#
# 👉 If you want to customize any of the default actions,
# simply uncomment the method definition below and modify it as needed.
# These are provided as templates to reduce boilerplate, not as restrictions.
#
module Api
